libintrons.py
extras.py
	Modules, imported by various scripts.
	libintrons.py contains the GenomicSequence class and all its subclasses,
	functions for deserializing GFF & FASTA, as well as scoring introns, plus
	some miscellaneous functions.
	extras.py contains various one-off functions.
	Which file contains what functions is kind of arbitrary.

add_introns.py
	Given a GFF & FASTA, interpose introns between each pair of exons.
	The introns will have their splice sites denoted as the "splice_site"
	attribute.

find_altseq_gff.py
	Given a GFF & FASTA and a file containing grouped genes, find pairs of
	transcript sequences which came from the same transcript.

find_altseq_fa.py
	Like find_altseq_fa.py, but takes only a FASTA file as input, and compares
	all unique pairs of sequences.

find_mrna_mismatches.py
	Given a transcriptome-to-genome mapping GFF, a genome FASTA and a
	transcriptome FASTA, find mappings whose sequences do not match the
	original transcript sequence.

get_orf_len.py
	Given a GFF & FASTA, report the length of each transcript's longest.

rectify_introns.py
	Given a GFF & FASTA, find and score all intron variants, then select the
	best variant for each intron. 

get_gene_scores.py
	Report the "avg_intron_score" attribute for every gene in a GFF file.

introns_corn.py
	Given a GFF, mark each intron with a "splice_site" attribute as
	conventional or nonconventional based on the splice site sequence.

subset_gff.py
	Given a GFF & a list of feature IDs, subset the GFF file to exclude 
	include the listed features and all of their children.
	Assumes every feature in the GFF with a Parent attribute comes after its
	parent.
	